# Local-only working notes. Both files say "never commit it" in their first
# line, and until now that was enforced only by .git/info/exclude — a file
# that lives in one working copy and travels with no clone. A fresh checkout
# on another machine would have committed them.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Built tarballs from `npm pack`. dist/ is ignored, the tarball that wraps it
# was not, so a stray clawgram-<version>.tgz sat untracked in the root asking
# to be committed by an `git add -A` somewhere.
*.tgz
